1
00:00:11,538 --> 00:00:17,538
Fast X: Part 2 is a action, crime, thriller film directed by Louis Leterrier.

2
00:00:23,076 --> 00:00:29,076
The eleventh installment in The Fast Saga, and a direct sequel to "Fast X".

3
00:00:34,615 --> 00:00:40,615
Dominic Toretto, played by Vin Diesel.

4
00:00:46,153 --> 00:00:52,153
Letty Ortiz, played by Michelle Rodriguez.

5
00:00:57,692 --> 00:01:03,692
Roman Pearce, played by Tyrese Gibson.

6
00:01:09,230 --> 00:01:15,230
Tej Parker, played by Ludacris.

7
00:01:20,769 --> 00:01:26,769
Ramsey, played by Nathalie Emmanuel.

8
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:38,307
Mia Toretto, played by Jordana Brewster.

9
00:01:43,846 --> 00:01:49,846
Fast X (also known as Fast & Furious 10) is a 2023 American action film directed by Louis Leterrier from a
screenplay by Dan Mazeau and Justin Lin, both of whom also co-wrote the story with Zach Dean.

10
00:01:55,384 --> 00:02:01,384
The sequel to F9 (2021), it is the tenth main installment and the
eleventh installment overall in the Fast & Furious franchise.

11
00:02:06,923 --> 00:02:12,923
It stars Vin Diesel as Dominic Toretto, alongside Michelle Rodriguez, Tyrese Gibson, Ludacris, John Cena, Nathalie Emmanuel, Jordana Brewster, Sung Kang,
Scott Eastwood, Daniela Melchior, Alan Ritchson, Helen Mirren, Brie Larson, Rita Moreno, Jason Statham, Jason Momoa, and Charlize Theron.

12
00:02:18,461 --> 00:02:24,461
In the film, Toretto must protect his family from Dante Reyes (Momoa), who
pursues revenge for his father's death and the loss of their fortune.

13
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Development on a tenth main Fast & Furious film began by
October 2020, with Lin returning to direct.

14
00:02:41,538 --> 00:02:47,538
The film's official title was revealed when
principal photography began in April 2022.

15
00:02:53,076 --> 00:02:59,076
Lin left as director later that month, citing creative differences,
though he retained writing and producing credits.

16
00:03:04,615 --> 00:03:10,615
Leterrier was then hired as his replacement a week later and
performed several uncredited rewrites to the screenplay.

17
00:03:16,153 --> 00:03:22,153
Longtime franchise composer Brian Tyler returned to score the film.

18
00:03:27,692 --> 00:03:33,692
With an estimated net production budget of $378.8 million, Fast
X is the sixth-most expensive film ever made.

19
00:03:39,230 --> 00:03:45,230
Filming lasted until that August, taking place in
London, Rome, Turin, Lisbon, and Los Angeles.

20
00:03:50,769 --> 00:03:56,769
Fast X premiered in Rome on May 12, 2023, and was released in the
United States on May 19, by Universal Pictures.

21
00:04:02,307 --> 00:04:08,307
The film received mixed reviews from critics, with praise for its action
sequences and Momoa's performance but criticism towards the writing.

22
00:04:13,846 --> 00:04:19,846
It grossed $714 million worldwide, becoming the
fifth-highest-grossing film of 2023.

23
00:04:25,384 --> 00:04:31,384
A sequel that reportedly serves as the final main installment is in
development and is scheduled to be released in April 2027.

24
00:04:36,923 --> 00:04:42,923
The film explores themes of sequel, racing, family, cars.

25
00:04:48,461 --> 00:04:54,461
The tone is intense.
